  "description": "HURRIY crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C86 H92 Fe6 Gd4 N34 O64,2(C2 H3 N1),C1 H2 Cl2,6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Gd1F (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2F (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1F (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe2F (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe3F (Fe) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.153-3.856 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.86-131.64°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C91Cl2H112Fe6Gd4N36O70. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
